ap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Questionnaire used in this study</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-24-20-i001"/></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Characteristics of 103 adolescent girls</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-24-20-i002"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>, kg/m<sup>2</sup>; <sup>&#x02020;</sup>, Seventy nine girls of total 103 could remember body weight and height at her menarche; <sup>&#x02021;</sup>, Atopic dermatitis, allergic rhinitis or urticaria.</p><p>BMI, body mass index.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Pulmonary function tests in adolescent girls association with obesity in 103 adolescent girls</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-24-20-i003"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>, Statistical significances were evaluated by student t-test.</p><p>BMI, body mass index.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Changes of pulmonary function test results according to menstrual cycle (N=51) in 103 adolescent girls</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-24-20-i004"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>, Statistical significances were evaluated by student t-test.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T5" position="float"><label>Table 5</label><caption><p>Results of pulmonary function test in 6 patients with a history of perimenstrual asthma</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-24-20-i005"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup>, Statistical significances were evaluated by Wilcoxon signed rank test.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>